JUDGMENT
Direct projectors preserve exact Date values, omit expiresAt for permanent events, retain agentId/scope/scopeRef, and upsert one insert-only record. A second projection does not duplicate or clobber text/expiry.
REFUTED at the manager seam: resolveWriteExpiresAt correctly gives explicit override priority and derives sessionDays expiry, and stored events carry it, but both manager projection payloads omit it. Therefore the real write path creates immortal chunks.
Because projection uses $setOnInsert only, a later repair projection cannot backfill expiresAt onto an already-created immortal chunk; remediation needs an update/backfill path, not only adding expiresAt to future manager payloads.
